Kit interface is stable (P1, proven on fab-line). Import from '../kit/<file>'.

sound.ts: call `useSound(lab)` once in your entry (arms the gesture gate, applies lab.chrome to the default: off in embedded and under reduced motion, on in /lab; the shell's pill toggles localStorage `lab-sound`). Then `play(name)` anywhere, including inside sim steps and useFrame: names are tick, page, pick, drawer, seat, toss, servo, chirp, zap, copy, swap, error; each is throttled. `hum(level 0..1)` drives the belt hum (call every frame with queue length / 3). `play` is a no-op before the first pointerdown/keydown and while muted; the AudioContext is created on the first unmuted play. `document.documentElement.dataset.sound` reads off | armed | on for harness evals. Do not play on camera moves.

a11y.tsx: render `<Mirror lab={lab} title="Your variant" />` last inside your root div (sr-only until it holds focus, then docks at the right; renders count, setup selects, command, and one aria-pressed button per item with id itemId(ref) and data-ref; announces adds/removes). Call `announce('X seated on the board, 3 parts')` from your seat event. `const keys = useSceneKeys({ lab, label, items: () => refs in grid order, cols })` and spread `keys.props` on your scene container (gives tabIndex, role=application, aria-activedescendant, data-focus-ref, arrows/Enter/Space/Escape). Inside the Canvas add `<FocusRing focus={keys.focusRef} locate={(ref, out) => radius or 0} color={accent} />`. Put `sceneFocusClass` on the scene container's className, and give that container its own position (`relative` or `absolute inset-0`); the class sets none: it draws the keyboard focus ring on an overlay pseudo-element, because an inset ring on the container paints beneath an opaque canvas (found by director-v2). `prefersReducedMotion()` / `useReducedMotion()` are here too.

perf.tsx: inside the Canvas add `<FrameGovernor busy={() => boolean} />` (switches to demand frameloop, full rate while busy() or within 700 ms of pointer/key input, else 30 Hz, 4 Hz under reduced motion; adapts dpr from hot frames only) and `<PerfProbe />` (writes calls, tris, frame, fps, dpr onto the canvas element's dataset every 0.5 s). Give the Canvas `dpr={dprRange()}` (caps 1.5 on coarse pointers). `busy()` must return true while anything in your sim or camera is still easing. `disposeTree(object3d)` frees geometry, materials and their textures.

touch.ts: `const { guard, props } = useSceneGestures({ onOrbit(dx, dy), onZoom(factor, x, y), onPan, onTap, onLongPress(x, y), onReset, onInteract })`; spread `props` on the scene container (sets touch-action none). Tap vs drag threshold is 4 px mouse / 10 px touch; `guard.moved` is true after a drag or a long press so mesh onClick handlers can ignore the click that follows; two fingers pinch (factor > 1 zooms in) and pan; wheel zooms; double tap or double click resets.

mobile.tsx: `useViewport()` gives { phone, touch, landscape, width, height }. `<Sheet label peek actions open onToggle>children</Sheet>` is a bottom sheet with the home-indicator safe area; put the call sheet, search and knobs in it on phones and hide the floating panels. The root viewport meta lacks viewport-fit=cover, so env(safe-area-inset-*) reads 0 until the morning (see REQUESTS.md).

Harness: scratchpad/p1/shot.ts (bun, run from that folder) adds --touch, --reduced, --sound on|off, --steps-file, and steps tap, press, pinch, swipe, focus, type, metrics, fps; window.__audioCtx counts AudioContext constructions.
